        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): keep element text truncation UTF-16 safe in cursor interactive elements",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`findCursorInteractiveElements` truncates DOM element text at 101 characters using `.slice(0, 101)`. When the 101st character is in the middle of an emoji (surrogate pair), the result contains a lone high surrogate, producing malformed Unicode.\n\nThe same file already imports and correctly uses `truncateUtf16Safe` at line 659, but this truncation site was missed.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `extensions/browser/src/browser/cdp.ts:641`: `.trim().slice(0, 101)` → `truncateUtf16Safe(..., 101)`\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Unit test (1/1 passed):**\n```\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  1 passed | 43 skipped (44)\n```\n\n**Lint:** `npx oxlint` — no errors\n\n**Type check:** `pnpm tsgo` — no errors\n\n**Real process proof (truncateUtf16Safe vs slice at boundary):**\n```\nHost: LIN-66D8BD4EA2C\nPID: 3364391\nTime: 2026-07-15T07:34:20.254Z\n\nInput: \"aaa...aaa😀b\" (103 chars, emoji at position 100)\n\n=== Before: slice(0, 101) ===\n  Result length: 101\n  Last char code: d83d\n  Has lone surrogate: true\n  → BROKEN: high surrogate without matching low surrogate\n\n=== After: truncateUtf16Safe(text, 101) ===\n  Result length: 100\n  Has lone surrogate: false\n  → VALID: emoji dropped whole, no broken Unicode\n```\n\n**Diff:**\n```diff\n-            text: String(el.textContent || \"\").replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").trim().slice(0, 101),\n+            text: truncateUtf16Safe(String(el.textContent || \"\").replace(/[ \\t\\n\\r\\f\\v]+/g, \" \").trim(), 101),\n```\n\nSame pattern as #107718 (recently merged gateway worker fix).\n\n## Review\n- Manually reviewed and verified\n- AI-assisted: Yes\n\n",
